{"term":"ابن القحبة","lang":"ar","script":"arab","romanization":"ibn al-qaḥba","category":"insults","subcategory":"maternal_whore","concept":"son_of_a_bitch_insult","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":95,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":95,"recognition_pct_peak":95,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"'Son of a whore'; severe maternal-lineage insult invoking the mother's alleged prostitution, functionally equivalent to English 'son of a bitch' but more sexually explicit due to the explicit prostitution lexeme.","english_term":"son of a whore","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"القحبة (prostitute) is itself highly offensive; the compound attacks maternal honor via sexual accusation; القحبة is more explicitly sexual than English 'bitch'; pan-Arabic recognition across all dialects."}
{"term":"ابن الكلبة","lang":"ar","script":"arab","romanization":"ibn al-kalba","category":"insults","subcategory":"maternal_animal","concept":"son_of_a_bitch_insult","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":80,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":96,"recognition_pct_peak":96,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"'Son of a female dog/bitch'; the most literal Arabic equivalent of English 'son of a bitch,' attacking the mother's honor through animal comparison rather than sexual accusation.","english_term":"son of a bitch","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Structurally and semantically the closest Arabic analog to English SOB; كلبة (female dog) maps directly to 'bitch'; somewhat less sexually loaded than ابن القحبة because the insult is animal-based rather than prostitution-based."}
{"term":"ابن الزانية","lang":"ar","script":"arab","romanization":"ibn al-zāniya","category":"insults","subcategory":"maternal_adulteress","concept":"son_of_a_bitch_insult","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":88,"technical":15,"recognition_pct_current":88,"recognition_pct_peak":88,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"'Son of a fornicatress/adulteress'; insult invoking the mother's alleged commission of zinā — the Islamic legal category for all unlawful sexual intercourse — compounding sexual slur with religious-moral condemnation.","english_term":"son of a whore","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"الزانية is the feminine active participle of زنا (zinā); carries heavier religious-legal weight than القحبة because zinā is a Quranic concept and a ḥadd offense in classical Islamic law; deployed when the speaker wants a religiously-framed insult rather than a purely crude one."}
{"term":"ابن المومس","lang":"ar","script":"arab","romanization":"ibn al-mūmis","category":"insults","subcategory":"maternal_prostitute","concept":"son_of_a_bitch_insult","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":85,"technical":10,"recognition_pct_current":80,"recognition_pct_peak":80,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"'Son of a prostitute'; maternal-lineage insult using مومس, a slightly more literary or formal register term for a prostitute or sexually loose woman.","english_term":"son of a whore","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"مومس is a step more elevated in register than قحبة, making this compound marginally less raw but still severe; more likely to appear in written or literary invective; recognition lower than ابن القحبة because مومس is a less everyday lexeme."}
{"term":"يا منيوك","lang":"ar","script":"arab","romanization":"yā manyūk","category":"insults","subcategory":"passive_sex_recipient","concept":"gay_man_slur","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":96,"technical":10,"recognition_pct_current":90,"recognition_pct_peak":90,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"'You who has been fucked/sodomized'; passive participle of نيك (to fuck) used as a severe insult implying the addressee has been used as a passive sexual object, with strong connotations of homosexual receptive role and profound emasculation.","english_term":"fucked one / sodomized one","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"In Arabic honor culture the passive-receptive sexual role is deeply stigmatizing; the insult attacks both sexual identity and masculine honor simultaneously; stronger than most English gay slurs because it combines a sexual-act accusation with an honor violation encoded in grammatical voice (passive participle = acted upon, not acting)."}
{"term":"يا عاهر","lang":"ar","script":"arab","romanization":"yā ʿāhir","category":"insults","subcategory":"fornication_accusation","concept":"fornicator","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"moral_religious","crude":70,"technical":20,"recognition_pct_current":88,"recognition_pct_peak":88,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"'O fornicator/whoremonger' (masculine form); insult from the root عهر denoting habitual illicit sexual conduct, applied to men who engage in or facilitate sexual immorality.","english_term":"fornicator / whoremonger","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Masculine counterpart to عاهرة (item 25); the word straddles moral condemnation and crude insult — carries Quranic-register gravity but is deployed conversationally; less common as a pure insult than its feminine form because female sexual transgression is more heavily stigmatized."}
{"term":"بظر أمك","lang":"ar","script":"arab","romanization":"baẓr ummak","category":"insults","subcategory":"maternal_anatomy","concept":"maternal_genital_insult","is_novel_concept":true,"register":"slang_crude","crude":99,"technical":28,"recognition_pct_current":85,"recognition_pct_peak":85,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"'Your mother's clitoris'; extreme honor-attack insult that names a female relative's genitalia by anatomical term as a form of maximal disrespect; the clitoris-specific variant of Arabic maternal genital cursing.","english_term":null,"english_translation_quality":"none","notes":"بظر is the semi-anatomical term for clitoris (relatively specific vs. the broader كس); the insult's mechanism is unique to the Arabic honor-shame framework — verbal exposure of maternal anatomy constitutes a grave attack on the family's honor; no English equivalent combines the maternal framing with specific anatomical naming as an insult genre; less universal than كس أمك but still widely recognized."}
{"term":"كس أمك","lang":"ar","script":"arab","romanization":"kuss ummak","category":"insults","subcategory":"maternal_anatomy","concept":"maternal_genital_insult","is_novel_concept":true,"register":"slang_crude","crude":100,"technical":18,"recognition_pct_current":98,"recognition_pct_peak":98,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"'Your mother's vagina/cunt'; the single most recognized and most offensive maternal genital insult in Arabic, invoking the mother's vagina as a catastrophic honor violation and general expletive.","english_term":null,"english_translation_quality":"none","notes":"كس is the most taboo sexual lexeme in Arabic; this two-word construction is likely the most widely recognized profanity across the entire Arabic-speaking world, understood universally across all dialects; used both as a directed insult and as a free-floating expletive of shock or frustration; recognition effectively 100% among adult Arabic speakers regardless of education or region."}
{"term":"أير في أمك","lang":"ar","script":"arab","romanization":"ayr fī ummak","category":"insults","subcategory":"maternal_sex_curse","concept":"motherfucker_insult","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":99,"technical":14,"recognition_pct_current":88,"recognition_pct_peak":88,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"'A penis in your mother'; extreme honor-attack curse phrased as a declarative verbless sentence invoking someone penetrating the addressee's mother, functionally equivalent to calling someone a motherfucker but structurally framed as a curse rather than a label.","english_term":"motherfucker","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"أير is a crude colloquial term for penis; the verbless-sentence construction (noun phrase as curse) is distinctly Arabic — it asserts an act rather than labeling the person, making it structurally different from the English 'motherfucker' label; both target the same honor-violation mechanism; common across Levantine and Egyptian dialects."}
{"term":"ابن عرص","lang":"ar","script":"arab","romanization":"ibn ʿarṣ","category":"insults","subcategory":"cuckold_insult","concept":"cuckoldry","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":85,"technical":10,"recognition_pct_current":80,"recognition_pct_peak":80,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"'Son of a pimp/cuckold'; insult derived from عرص, denoting a man who profits from or is complicit in female family members' sexual dishonor — whether as a pimp, a passive facilitator, or a failed guardian — with the compound attacking the father's honor and virility.","english_term":"son of a pimp","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"عرص is semantically fluid across dialects: Egyptian usage leans toward 'pimp'; Levantine usage toward 'passive homosexual' or 'man dishonored through his women'; the paternal targeting distinguishes it from the maternal-lineage insults above; the concept intersects with dayyūth (item 19) but عرص more explicitly implies active exploitation or a passive-homosexual stigma."}
{"term":"يا لوطي","lang":"ar","script":"arab","romanization":"yā lūṭī","category":"insults","subcategory":"homosexual_slur","concept":"sodomite","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"moral_religious","crude":80,"technical":22,"recognition_pct_current":92,"recognition_pct_peak":92,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"'O sodomite/homosexual'; insult derived from the name of the Prophet Lūṭ (Lot), whose community was destroyed in the Quran for sexual transgression; the standard Islamic-register term for a gay man or sodomite, carrying both legal and theological condemnation.","english_term":"sodomite","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Direct Islamic parallel to the English 'sodomite': both derive from an Abrahamic narrative of divine punishment for homosexual acts; لوطية is the jurisprudential noun for the act in Islamic law; carries more formal-theological weight than يا منيوك; the Quranic backstory is actively part of its meaning in ways that 'sodomite' has largely lost in English secular usage."}
{"term":"يا زاني","lang":"ar","script":"arab","romanization":"yā zānī","category":"insults","subcategory":"fornication_accusation","concept":"fornicator","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"moral_religious","crude":65,"technical":22,"recognition_pct_current":92,"recognition_pct_peak":92,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"'O adulterer/fornicator'; accusation invoking zinā — the Islamic legal category covering all unlawful sexual intercourse — which carries both severe social condemnation and, under classical Islamic law, potential corporal punishment.","english_term":"adulterer / fornicator","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Zinā in Islamic jurisprudence covers all extra-marital sex regardless of marital status of the parties; the hadd punishment is 100 lashes for an unmarried person or death by stoning for a married person in classical fiqh, giving this insult a gravity the English 'fornicator' has entirely lost; theological weight makes it more potent in religious-conservative contexts than its moderate crude score suggests."}
{"term":"يا فاجر","lang":"ar","script":"arab","romanization":"yā fājir","category":"insults","subcategory":"moral_depravity","concept":"libertine","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"moral_religious","crude":55,"technical":15,"recognition_pct_current":82,"recognition_pct_peak":82,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"'O depraved/dissolute one'; insult from the root فجور (moral corruption, sexual licentiousness, sinfulness), broadly condemning someone as morally bankrupt with sexual immorality as the primary but not exclusive implication.","english_term":"libertine / debaucher","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"فاجر is broader than عاهر or زاني — it condemns general moral corruption including but not limited to sexual sins; also used in political and religious rhetoric against moral degeneracy; Quranic usage (البر والفجور) reinforces its gravity but makes it slightly more formal and less street-level crude than the other sexual insults in this section."}
{"term":"يا حمار","lang":"ar","script":"arab","romanization":"yā ḥimār","category":"insults","subcategory":"animal_stupidity","concept":"bastard_insult","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":38,"technical":4,"recognition_pct_current":99,"recognition_pct_peak":99,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"'O donkey/ass'; primarily a non-sexual insult meaning idiot or blockhead; listed here because in Arabic folk metaphor the donkey is also associated with large genitalia and unrestrained animal sexuality, giving it a secondary sexual register in some usages.","english_term":"jackass / dumbass","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"The weakest item in this list by crude score; primarily means 'you fool'; the sexual resonance is secondary and context-dependent; Arabic folk idiom associates the donkey with an oversized penis (أير الحمار), so in explicit sexual contexts the word gains a different valence; one of the most universally recognized insults in Arabic precisely because it is mild enough for semi-public use."}
{"term":"تيس","lang":"ar","script":"arab","romanization":"tays","category":"insults","subcategory":"lecherous_male","concept":"male_hypersexuality","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":52,"technical":4,"recognition_pct_current":90,"recognition_pct_peak":90,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"'Billy goat'; applied to a man as an insult meaning sexually voracious, lecherous, or uncontrollably lustful, evoking the male goat's notorious smell, rutting behavior, and indiscriminate sexuality.","english_term":"lecher / horny goat","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"The goat-as-lechery metaphor is cross-cultural but Arabic تيس carries additional semantic freight: in Islamic ritual context the تيس is an animal of sacrifice, adding a contempt dimension; can alternatively mean 'blockhead' or 'dunce' without sexual connotation depending on context; closer to English 'horny old goat' than to 'satyr' but evokes the same goat-lust archetype."}
{"term":"يا عرص","lang":"ar","script":"arab","romanization":"yā ʿarṣ","category":"insults","subcategory":"cuckold_insult","concept":"cuckoldry","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":83,"technical":10,"recognition_pct_current":80,"recognition_pct_peak":80,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"'O pimp/cuckold'; direct vocative use of عرص labeling the addressee as someone who exploits women sexually (pimp), fails to protect female family members' honor, or occupies the passive-homosexual role; strong connotations of emasculation.","english_term":"pimp / cuckold","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Direct usage without the 'son of' frame intensifies the insult as a personal label rather than a lineage attack; in Egyptian Arabic the pimp meaning dominates; in Levantine Arabic the passive-homosexual or dishonored-man-through-women reading is more salient; the word encapsulates the honor-shame economy where male worth derives from controlling female sexuality."}
{"term":"نيّاك","lang":"ar","script":"arab","romanization":"nayyāk","category":"insults","subcategory":"sexual_aggressor_insult","concept":"fucker_insult","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":90,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":85,"recognition_pct_peak":85,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"'Fucker'; intensive-pattern active participle of نيك (to fuck), labeling someone as an inveterate or aggressive sexual actor; used as a general crude insult comparable to English 'fucker.'","english_term":"fucker","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"The فعّال pattern in Arabic morphology denotes habitual or excessive agency — nayyāk means 'one who fucks constantly and aggressively'; paradoxically, in a culture that stigmatizes the passive role (منيوك), the active-voice label carries less pure sexual shame and is sometimes wielded with mixed swagger-and-insult connotations; one of the most morphologically transparent sex-derived insults in Arabic."}
{"term":"أبو طيز","lang":"ar","script":"arab","romanization":"abū ṭīz","category":"insults","subcategory":"buttocks_insult","concept":"asshole_insult","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":65,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":78,"recognition_pct_peak":78,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"'Father of an ass/butt'; colorful insult using the Arabic kunya (father-of) construction with طيز (buttocks) to label someone as contemptible or sexually crude via deliberate inversion of the honorific kunya form.","english_term":"asshole","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"طيز refers to buttocks broadly rather than the anus specifically, so the anatomical match to English 'asshole' is imprecise; the kunya construction (أبو X) is culturally honorific — using it with a crude body part creates deliberate comic and offensive inversion; more witty than devastating; more common in Egyptian and Levantine colloquial Arabic than in Gulf or Maghrebi dialects."}
{"term":"ديوث","lang":"ar","script":"arab","romanization":"dayyūth","category":"honor_shame_economy","subcategory":"ghayra_absent","concept":"dayyuth","is_novel_concept":true,"register":"moral_religious","crude":95,"technical":22,"recognition_pct_current":90,"recognition_pct_peak":90,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"A man who lacks protective sexual jealousy (ghayra) over his female relatives — wife, daughters, sisters, mother — and either permits, facilitates, or is indifferent to other men's sexual access to them; one of the most condemned categories in Islamic moral theology, barred from paradise in hadith.","english_term":null,"english_translation_quality":"none","notes":"The concept requires the Arabic honor-shame framework in which a man's worth depends on his exclusive control of his women's sexuality; ديوث is distinct from 'cuckold' (deceived without consent), 'pimp' (commercial exploitation), and 'hotwife husband' (consensual kink): it is specifically the willing or negligent abandonment of ghayra (غيرة, protective jealousy) as a moral-religious failure; cited in multiple hadith as a person Allah will not look upon on Judgment Day; no English word or concept adequately captures the theological and honor-economic weight of the term."}
{"term":"بنت الشوارع","lang":"ar","script":"arab","romanization":"bint al-shawāriʿ","category":"insults","subcategory":"slut_shame","concept":"promiscuous_woman_slur","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":78,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":93,"recognition_pct_peak":93,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"'Girl/daughter of the streets'; a slur for a woman of loose sexual morals or a prostitute, implying she belongs to no respectable household and is sexually available to any man she encounters on the street.","english_term":"streetwalker / woman of the streets","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"The 'streets' framing encodes the honor-shame logic: a proper woman is confined to the domestic sphere under male guardianship; a woman 'of the streets' has escaped that control and is therefore sexually available to all; sits between general promiscuity accusation and explicit prostitution accusation — the ambiguity intensifies the insult."}
{"term":"بنت الهوا","lang":"ar","script":"arab","romanization":"bint al-hawā","category":"insults","subcategory":"slut_shame","concept":"sex_worker_archaic","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"euphemism","crude":52,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":82,"recognition_pct_peak":82,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"'Girl of desire/air/whim'; a softer euphemism for a prostitute or sexually loose woman, using الهوى — which means carnal desire, romantic passion, or literally the wind — as a poetic veil over an explicit accusation.","english_term":"woman of pleasure / fallen woman","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"الهوى is beautifully ambiguous: it can mean erotic desire (هوى النفس), capricious whim, or simply air/breeze — the term lets speakers imply prostitution with plausible deniability; this makes it suitable for contexts where direct obscenity would be inappropriate; predominantly Egyptian colloquial usage; notably softer than بنت الشوارع while covering similar semantic ground."}
{"term":"سائبة","lang":"ar","script":"arab","romanization":"sāʾiba","category":"insults","subcategory":"slut_shame","concept":"sexual_permissiveness_pejorative","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":60,"technical":10,"recognition_pct_current":78,"recognition_pct_peak":78,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"'Stray/loose woman'; adjective-as-insult for a woman who is sexually available or promiscuous, derived from سائب (unattached, untethered, free-roaming), implying she lacks proper male guardianship and therefore sexual control.","english_term":"loose woman / strumpet","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"The root image is of an animal let off its leash — سائبة describes stray animals in standard usage; when applied to a woman it frames her sexual autonomy as dangerous freedom from rightful restraint; reflects the honor-shame framework in which female sexuality must be supervised by male guardians; moderate crude score because the animalistic comparison is implicit rather than explicit."}
{"term":"مبذولة","lang":"ar","script":"arab","romanization":"mabdhūla","category":"insults","subcategory":"slut_shame","concept":"sexual_permissiveness_pejorative","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":68,"technical":16,"recognition_pct_current":70,"recognition_pct_peak":70,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"'One who is freely given/offered'; passive participle of بذل (to give or spend liberally), applied to a woman to mean she makes herself sexually available to anyone without restriction, framing her body as a commodity dispensed without cost or gatekeeping.","english_term":"easy woman / sexually available woman","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"The passive-participle morphology (مفعولة pattern) is linguistically significant: it grammatically positions the woman as the object of action rather than the agent — she is 'given out' rather than actively choosing; slightly more formal or literary register than direct slurs; the commodity metaphor (بذل also applies to spending money freely) encodes the sexual economics implicit in honor-shame vocabulary."}
{"term":"هرّة","lang":"ar","script":"arab","romanization":"hirra","category":"insults","subcategory":"slut_shame","concept":"slut_shame_woman","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":55,"technical":4,"recognition_pct_current":70,"recognition_pct_peak":70,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"'Female cat'; used as a veiled slur for a promiscuous or sexually available woman, drawing on the cat's associations with nocturnal wandering, sexual heat cycles, and wanton behavior in Arabic folk idiom.","english_term":"loose woman / cat","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"The female-cat metaphor for female promiscuity is cross-cultural (cf. English 'pussy' and 'cat' in dated use) but operates somewhat differently in Arabic: the هرة in heat (الشبق) is a specific folk image; mild enough to be used in semi-polite company as a veiled insult where direct terms would be unacceptable; regional variation is significant — more common in Egyptian and Levantine colloquial than Gulf Arabic."}
{"term":"عاهرة","lang":"ar","script":"arab","romanization":"ʿāhira","category":"sex_work_pornography","subcategory":"prostitute_term","concept":"sex_worker","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":90,"technical":16,"recognition_pct_current":97,"recognition_pct_peak":97,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"'Whore/prostitute'; the most common and widely recognized Arabic word for a prostitute or sexually promiscuous woman, derived from the root عهر (habitual illicit sexual conduct); used both as a literal descriptor for sex workers and as a maximally offensive general insult.","english_term":"whore / prostitute","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Feminine active participle of عهر; among the most loaded terms in the Arabic lexicon, combining three registers simultaneously: religious (عهر appears in classical Islamic texts on sexual transgression), legal (historically a ḥadd-adjacent concept), and social (maximum female honor violation); the word's power exceeds the English 'whore' because in Arabic cultural context it implicates family honor, religious standing, and legal jeopardy together; ubiquitous as a general female insult well beyond literal application to sex workers."}
